(RSpec Execution Regression Post-Mortem) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Date: 2026-04-24 Status: Resolved Scope: RSpec integration, mutation) Tj
T*
(child execution, baseline coverage bootstrap, smoke coverage) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Summary) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Henitai regressed in its own RSpec execution path and became unable to) Tj
T*
(run mutation testing reliably on the Henitai repository itself. The) Tj
T*
(visible symptoms were:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- mutant children timing out) Tj
T*
(- child logs showing No examples found. or stopping after) Tj
T*
(  runner_run_start) Tj
T*
(- baseline coverage bootstrap failing intermittently on repo-scale runs) Tj
T*
(- real zero-example runs being misclassified) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The regression had two related technical causes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1.  The mutant child path had drifted away from the documented execution) Tj
T*
(    model. Mutation activation is process-local in Henitai, so the) Tj
T*
(    activated mutant and the test run must stay in the same forked child) Tj
T*
(    process. Earlier work had introduced an additional execution) Tj
T*
(    boundary and weakened that contract.) Tj
T*
(2.  The RSpec boot path relied on RSpec::Core::Runner.run\(...\) and) Tj
T*
(    related default discovery behavior in places where Henitai already) Tj
T*
(    had an explicit file list. On the Henitai repository this triggered) Tj
T*
(    expensive repo-scale discovery through) Tj
T*
(    Configuration#get_files_to_run, which was cheap enough on tiny smoke) Tj
T*
(    fixtures to go unnoticed but pathological on the real codebase.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The failure was not caused by mutation activation itself. It was caused) Tj
T*
(by an invalid execution workflow around RSpec boot and discovery.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Impact) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- bundle exec henitai run on the Henitai repository became unreliable or) Tj
T*
(  unusable.) Tj
T*
(- Mutation runs produced timeouts instead of actionable statuses.) Tj
T*
(- Diagnostic logs were initially too weak to separate real timeouts,) Tj
T*
(  discovery failures, and misclassification.) Tj
T*
(- Confidence in the basic RSpec integration dropped because toy smoke) Tj
T*
(  projects stayed green while the real repo failed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(User-Visible Symptoms) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Narrow dogfood runs like) Tj
T*
(  bundle exec henitai run 'Henitai::Integration' produced many T timeout) Tj
T*
(  results.) Tj
T*
(- Some mutant logs contained No examples found. even though the selected) Tj
T*
(  spec files existed and contained examples.) Tj
T*
(- Baseline coverage bootstrap failed with Henitai::CoverageError on the) Tj
T*
(  repo.) Tj
T*
(- The existing smoke suite reported:) Tj
T*
(  - smoke:rspec ok) Tj
T*
(  - smoke:minitest ok even while the real repository run was broken.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Detection) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The issue was detected by dogfooding Henitai against its own repository,) Tj
T*
(not by CI or by the existing integration smoke suite.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(That mattered. The existing smoke fixtures were real projects, but they) Tj
T*
(were too small to trigger the discovery cost and state problems that) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
